From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: decode Dolby VSVDB v2 target min/max as PQ codes

84c1fdbb12 ("amdv: parse DV VSVDB v2 target min/max luminance") enabled
FLAG_USE_SINK_MIN_MAX by default and added a ver == 2 branch that applies the
v1 formulas (max = 100 + 50 * CV nits, min = (CV/127)^2 nits) to the v2
tmaxPQ/tminPQ fields. hdmitx_edid_parse.c stores those as the raw 5-bit
fields (dat >> 3), and in VSVDB v2 they index 12-bit PQ code values:
max PQ = 2055 + 65 * idx, min PQ = 20 * idx. That is how linuxtv edid-decode
decodes v2 ("Target Max PQ v2"), and it matches what dovi.ko's own VSVDB
handling does with the same bytes.

Example, LG G6 VSVDB eb0146d000 4802b67e6c867c: max idx 22 = PQ 3485 = ~2485
nits; the v1 formula gave 1200. With the flag on that value replaces every
amdv_target_max entry, graphic_max/min and amdv_target_min, so it reaches the
VS10 DV->HDR10 target and the OSD graphics peak.

Keep the flag and the v2 branch; convert through precomputed ST 2084 tables
(no float in the kernel) at both sites.

--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -407,6 +407,23 @@
